 "text": "Hello there, how are you feeling today? It depends on the thinner the better. Two thin coats with an hour between them beats a single thick coat. That's a tight turn. If it' a big piece, hanging it up somewhere out of the way over night helps immensely. Spray poly works in few minutes, but it wears off quite fast. A thick brush based poli takes hours to dry completely, a week away at least. Touch dry feels dry to the touch, but the surface will still fog up completely drying it takes few days indoors, several outside on a warm day.",
